---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema, buildFAQSchema } from "../../lib/seo";

const pageFaqs = [
  {
    question: "What is CELPIP Speaking Task 2 testing?",
    answer:
      "Task 2 is testing whether you can tell a clear personal experience in a natural, organized way.",
  },
  {
    question: "How detailed should my Task 2 story be?",
    answer:
      "It should be detailed enough to feel real, but not so long that the story loses direction. One clear event is usually better than many scattered details.",
  },
  {
    question: "What usually lowers Task 2 scores?",
    answer:
      "Scores often drop when the story has no clear order, repeats the same idea, or ends before the main event is fully explained.",
  },
];

const pageStructuredData = [
  buildBreadcrumbSchema(Astro.site, [
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Blog", path: "/blog/" },
    { name: "CELPIP Speaking Task 2", path: "/blog/celpip-speaking-part2/" },
  ]),
  buildFAQSchema(pageFaqs),
];
---

<Layout
  title="CELPIP Speaking Task 2 | Tell a Personal Experience Clearly"
  description="A CELPIP Speaking Task 2 guide with personal-story structure, useful detail, and clearer ways to sound organized under time pressure."
  type="article"
  keywords="CELPIP Speaking Task 2, CELPIP personal experience, CELPIP speaking task 2 guide"
  structuredData={pageStructuredData}
>
  <article class="section guide-article">
    <a class="guide-back-link" href="/blog">Back to blog</a>

    <header class="guide-header">
      <span class="guide-tag">CELPIP speaking guide</span>
      <h1 style="margin: 0;">CELPIP Speaking Task 2</h1>
      <div class="guide-meta">
        <span>March 17, 2026</span>
        <span>7 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="guide-lead">
      <p>
        CELPIP Speaking Task 2 asks you to talk about a personal experience. The safest
        answer is not the most dramatic story. It is the clearest one. If the listener can
        follow the story easily, your answer already sounds stronger.
      </p>
      <p>
        Focus on one experience, one sequence of events, and one clear ending.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-grid guide-grid-2">
      <section class="guide-card">
        <h2>What to include</h2>
        <ul class="guide-list">
          <li>Where and when the experience happened.</li>
          <li>What the main event was.</li>
          <li>What happened in the end.</li>
          <li>Why the experience still matters to you.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-card">
        <h2>What to avoid</h2>
        <ul class="guide-list">
          <li>Starting with too much background.</li>
          <li>Jumping from one event to another without order.</li>
          <li>Repeating the same feeling again and again.</li>
          <li>Ending suddenly without a result or reflection.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>A simple Task 2 story frame</h2>
      <div class="guide-steps">
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Set the context</h3>
            <p>Say when it happened and who was involved.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Describe the main event</h3>
            <p>Tell the most important part of the story clearly and directly.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Give the result</h3>
            <p>Explain what happened after the event.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">4</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Finish with reflection</h3>
            <p>Say why you remember it or what you learned from it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>A short answer frame</h2>
      <div class="guide-example">
        <p><strong>Context:</strong> I would like to talk about an experience I had when...</p>
        <p><strong>Main event:</strong> The most memorable part was when...</p>
        <p><strong>Result:</strong> In the end, ...</p>
        <p><strong>Reflection:</strong> I still remember this experience because...</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>What often sounds weak</h2>
      <table class="guide-mistake-table">
        <tr>
          <th>Weak move</th>
          <th>Better move</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The story starts too far from the real event.</td>
          <td>Reach the main event early.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The speaker gives disconnected details.</td>
          <td>Use clear time order: first, then, after that, finally.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The story feels unfinished.</td>
          <td>Add the result and one final reflection.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The answer sounds memorized.</td>
          <td>Use a structure, but keep the wording natural.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>Next step</h2>
      <div class="guide-links">
        <a href="/blog/celpip-speaking-task-1">
          <strong>Read the Task 1 guide</strong>
          <span>Compare personal storytelling with giving advice.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/blog/celpip-speaking-task-7-opinion-strategy">
          <strong>Read the Task 7 opinion guide</strong>
          <span>Move from storytelling to clear opinion speaking.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/celpip/speaking">
          <strong>Go to the CELPIP speaking hub</strong>
          <span>Find more speaking guides and related lessons.</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <div class="guide-faq">
        {pageFaqs.map((item) => (
          <details class="card">
            <summary>{item.question}</summary>
            <p class="muted" style="margin-top: var(--s-2); margin-bottom: 0;">{item.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
